  "objects": "E,S,V,kappa,eta,y; one existential measurable p; residual rho_s; actual base tilt mu and quadratic second tilt R_s; actual affine pushforward r_s; covariance-identity gamma; literal Z_s,q_s,f_s.",
  "domains": "E is a complete finite-dimensional real Hilbert space with its Borel structure, dimension zero allowed. S is an arbitrary measurable space. V:E->R; kappa:R with kappa>=1; eta:S->R with every value positive; y,p:S->E; rho_s,q_s,f_s:E->R. mu,R_s,r_s,gamma are measures on E. L2 domains are gamma for f_s and grad f_s, r_s for grad rho_s; q_s log q_s is integrated under gamma.",
  "quantifiers": "Universal E,S,V,kappa,eta,y satisfying hypotheses; Hessian inequalities hold for all x,v. There exists one measurable p such that the stationary equation holds for all s, and all later definitions use that same p. Thereafter for every s all listed conclusions hold, with pointwise identities for all u. There is no restriction on cardinality or nonemptiness of S.",
