  "conclusion": "Existence of measurable p solving p_s+eta_s grad V(p_s)=y_s; for each s, positive Z_s<=1; the actual tilted-law affine pushforward r_s equals the residual Gaussian tilt and its literal q_s density; r_s probability; q_s>0 and f_s2=q_s pointwise; q_s normalized under gamma; C2 f_s; specified L2 and entropy integrability; both pointwise gradient identities; exact energy equality with coefficient 1/4.",
  "scopes": "A parameterized theorem over arbitrary measurable S, not only fixed eta,y. Each eta_s may be arbitrarily large while remaining positive. The stationary p is shared across residual potential and affine map. map denotes actual pushforward of the two-stage normalized tilt. Smoothness and gradients are in u in E, not in S. No explicit uniqueness or joint-parameter smoothness conclusion appears; no convergence rate or entropy upper bound appears.",
